> Yes, we need native IM support. grinev/opencode-telegram-bot is a good project, but can't render the session on terminal, desktop and mobile phone at same time.

@freezed-corpse-143 I've implemented this feature in latest release. But OpenCode CLI should be launched with --port option to have exact port and bot can connect to it. Or OpenCode CLI should be launched with attach option to connect to the same opencode server as bot. I haven't found a way around this limitation, OpenСode always runs the server on a random port by default.
Otherwise, the feature is fully functional and the session progress is displayed simultaneously in both the bot and the cli.

@m13v this feels incredibly validating lol. thank you for commenting.

I think inject vs send can be configured to user preference but I've found that Anthropic models are generally pretty good at sussing out dictation errors if you specify that you're using dictation in AGENTS.md (or equivalent).

As long as the core functionality is available, it can be configured in the respective plugins.

reposting from the discord so people can find it -> local-alias@tarball-url should work for those who can't wait/need it right meow. somewhat contrived but eg.

`{
  "plugin": [
    "antigravity-auth@https://registry.npmjs.org/opencode-antigravity-auth/-/opencode-antigravity-auth-1.6.0.tgz"
  ]
}`

works the same for private registries
